<title>USA: Israel Land corrects Q3 dollar results.</title>
<headline>Israel Land corrects Q3 dollar results.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel Land Development Co Ltd said Monday the U.S. dollar version of its third quarter results released November 26 was based on an incorrect exchange rate for new Israeli shekels.</p>
<p>The company reported the following corrected results.</p>
<p>Dollars in thousands, except share and per share data</p>
<p>			Nine Months Ended	 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>		     9/30/96     9/30/95	9/30/96     9/30/95</p>
<p> Revenue	   $221,196   $208,236	$ 75,299   $ 66,646</p>
<p>Capital Gains</p>
<p>  (Losses) Net	3,502	  186		11	  (17)</p>
<p> Total		224,698    208,422	  75,310     66,629</p>
<p> Net Income	   3,853	5,535	     853	  716</p>
<p> Net Per Share	 0.14	 0.20	    0.03	 0.02</p>
<p>Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding 28,268,823  28,268,823   28,268,823  28,268,823</p>
<p>Note: All US$ figures represent translations using an exchange rate of 3.22 New Israeli Shekels (NIS) to US $1.00 as of September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>This corrects the exchange rate from the 2.995 shekels per dollar used November 26.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
